; List the visible exits of a location
;
; Prints "Visible exits are:" and the direction word of every exit that has no
; obstacle and is not erased (#R$A124), then a new line. Prints nothing when
; there is no such exit. Part of every location description (#R$965B), after
; the obstacles (#R$A0C8); also the second entry of that description at $967F.
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
;
; A Location id
; Preserves BC, DE, IX and IY.
@label=ListVisibleExits
c$A138 PUSH IX
 $A13A PUSH IY
 $A13C PUSH DE
 $A13D PUSH BC
 $A13E CALL $A0AE    ; IX = location record + 7, BC = 3
 $A141 CALL $A124    ; IX = first listable exit
 $A144 JR Z,$A15D    ; none: print nothing
 $A146 LD HL,$B020   ; "Visible exits are:"
 $A149 CALL $72DD
@label=ListVisibleExits_Next
*$A14C LD A,(IX+$00) ; direction id of the exit
 $A14F CALL $A0BA    ; DE = direction word
 $A152 CALL $74C1    ; print the word
 $A155 CALL $A124    ; next listable exit
 $A158 JR NZ,$A14C
 $A15A CALL $8583    ; end the line
*$A15D POP BC
 $A15E POP DE
 $A15F POP IY
 $A161 POP IX
 $A163 RET
